  "worked_solution": "We transfer the negative into the numerator of the fraction, and proceed with cross-multiplication:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{y+5}{3} & =\\frac{4y+3}{5} \\\\ \\frac{-(y+5)}{3} & =\\frac{4y+3}{5} \\\\ \\frac{-y-5}{3} & =\\frac{4y+3}{5} \\\\ (-y-5)\\cdot 5 & =3\\cdot (4y+3)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we proceed as usual to solve the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-y-5)\\cdot 5 & =3\\cdot (4y+3) \\\\ -5y-25 & =12y+9 \\\\ -5y-25+5y & =12y+9+5y \\\\ -25 & =17y+9 \\\\ -25-9 & =17y+9-9 \\\\ -34 & =17y \\\\ \\frac{-34}{17} & =\\frac{17y}{17} \\\\ -2 & =y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, $y=-2.$",
